"""Run the LXD integration targets and scenarios on nested LXD sandboxes.

The runner lives in a container on the test server. It creates one sandbox VM per slot
with the host LXD, runs targets and scenarios against the sandboxes, and deletes them.
It uses only the Python standard library and the lxc client.

The remote and the project have no built-in default. The runner reads them, in this order, from
--remote and --project, from LXDTEST_REMOTE and LXDTEST_PROJECT, or from /etc/lxdtest/config.json.
ci/bootstrap.py writes that file. LXDTEST_CONFIG names another file.
"""

